defaults.scene_start_update_prompt_template:
A scene transition has just been detected -- the LATEST exchange opens the NEW scene. The `start` block of current_scene still describes the PREVIOUS scene's opening and must be COMPLETELY REWRITTEN to describe the new scene's opening. The `now` block must be RESET to that same opening moment. The `what` field must be rewritten to describe the new scene.
Relevant Schema:
```json
{{ schema_snippet }}
```

Example JSON structure:
```json
{{ example_json }}
```

If updates are needed, provide a list of changes. Each change must specify the 'path' to the field and the 'value' for the update. The path is a dot-separated str relative to current_scene, using numeric indices or square brackets for list items (e.g. 'start.who.characters.0.location').

You MUST provide updates covering ALL of the following, rewritten from the new scene's opening exchange:
- {"path": "what", "value": "<one-line summary of the new scene's opening>"}
- {"path": "start.where", "value": "<new scene location>"}
- {"path": "start.when.date", "value": "<date or 'N/A'>"}
- {"path": "start.when.time", "value": "<general time of day>"}
- {"path": "start.when.specific_time", "value": "<precise time or 'N/A'>"}
- {"path": "start.when._message_node", "value": "{{ current_message_node }}"}
- {"path": "start.who.characters", "value": [{"name": "<name>", "location": "<location>"}]}, plus groups and elements lists similarly if anyone is present
- {"path": "start.why", "value": [{"name": "<reason title>", "details": "<why they are here>"}]}
- The SAME opening values under the parallel `now.*` paths: now.who / now.when / now.where / now.why -- so Scene Start and Scene Now render identically at the boundary. The `now.when.specific_time` must be concrete and grounded in the opening exchange.

If the latest exchange does NOT open a new scene after all, respond with the exact str: NO_UPDATES_REQUIRED

REMEMBER: Provide your response in the specified JSON format or the 'NO_UPDATES_REQUIRED' str, not the entry object as a whole. Do NOT set any engine-meta key (`_scene_number`, `_scene_start_message`, `_chapter_number`, `_arc_number`) except `start.when._message_node`.

